## 2026-09-23 00:20 IST — Approved Fix: Tighten Authoritative Media Completion Check (Exact uploadRequestId Matching)

### Why this work was requested
- A pre-commit safety review revealed that determining media completion via asset count comparison (`serverAssets.length >= expectedCount`) inside `handleRetryCardMedia()` was insufficiently authoritative:
  - If a listing already possessed legacy or unrelated media assets on the server (e.g. `OLD_X`, `OLD_Y`, plus 1 uploaded asset `A`), `serverAssets.length` would equal 3, satisfying `3 >= 3` even when expected staged media `B` and `C` were missing.
  - This could cause premature reconciliation into `completedListings` and false `Published` state while media was incomplete.

### Canonical Identity Contract
- Each staged-media item has durable identity (`item.id` or `(item.file as any)?.draftMediaId`).
- Canonical upload request IDs are generated deterministically via `createStableUploadRequestId(card.publishedId, item.file, durableDraftMediaId)`.
- Server `PropertyMediaAsset` entities expose `uploadRequestId`.
- Authoritative completion requires that **every single expected staged-media `uploadRequestId` exists in the set of server media `uploadRequestId`s**. Extra unrelated server assets do not prevent completion, but missing even one expected asset prevents completion.

### Files Modified
- `frontend-web/src/components/BatchPropertyIngestionStudio.tsx`:
  - In `handleRetryCardMedia`, replaced count check (`serverAssets.length >= expectedCount`) with strict set membership check:
    ```typescript
    const publishedListingId = card.publishedId;
    let allMediaPersisted = false;
    try {
      const serverAssets = await propertyService.fetchTaggedMedia(publishedListingId);
      if (Array.isArray(serverAssets)) {
        const existingReqIds = new Set(
          serverAssets.map((asset) => asset.uploadRequestId).filter(Boolean) as string[]
        );
        allMediaPersisted = (card.stagedMedia || []).every((item) => {
          const durableMediaId = item.id || (item.file as any)?.draftMediaId;
          const expectedReqId = createStableUploadRequestId(
            publishedListingId,
            item.file,
            durableMediaId
          );
          return existingReqIds.has(expectedReqId);
        });
      }
    } catch (err) {
      console.warn('[handleRetryCardMedia] Could not verify permanent media assets on server:', err);
    }
    ```
- `frontend-web/src/tests/partiallyPublishedCardRecovery.test.mjs`:
  - Updated existing retry tests 14, 16, 17 to use realistic `uploadRequestId` matching.
  - Added deterministic regression tests A–E (tests 19–23):
    - Test 19 (TEST A): Exact IDs complete (`A, B, C` present -> reconciliation allowed).
    - Test 20 (TEST B - CRITICAL REGRESSION): Extra unrelated media (`OLD_X, OLD_Y, A` where count `3 >= 3` is satisfied but `B` and `C` are missing -> NOT complete, NO reconciliation, card remains staged, NO false Published state).
    - Test 21 (TEST C): Extra media + all expected IDs (`OLD_X, A, B, C, OLD_Y` -> complete, reconciliation allowed; unrelated assets do not interfere).
    - Test 22 (TEST D): One expected ID missing (`A, C` present, `B` missing -> NOT complete, card remains staged).
    - Test 23 (TEST E): Backend already completed race (server already contains all expected uploadRequestIds -> deduplication skips re-upload, authoritative verification succeeds, card reconciles as Published).

### Verification Results
